<p>On August 25, 1778, a merchant named Haym Salomon wrote a letter to the Continental Congress in Philadelphia. He had escaped from British-held New York a few days before. In the letter he said that he had lost all his property. He had left his wife and a month-old baby behind in the city. He asked Congress for one thing, a job in his line of business.</p>
