<p>Salem enlisted again and again. In 1776 he fought at Harlem Heights and Trenton. In 1777 he signed up for three more years and was at Saratoga. In 1779 he was at Stony Point, where American light infantry stormed a British fort on the Hudson River at night. His service ended on March 1, 1780, almost five years after he marched to Concord.</p>
