<p>In the Georgia backcountry the Revolution was a civil war. Neighbors who supported the king, called <strong>Loyalists</strong> or Tories, fought neighbors who supported independence, called Patriots or Whigs. Both sides raided each other's farms. Loyalists called the area the Hornet's Nest because so many people there backed independence.</p>
