<p>In October 1776 Arnold built a small fleet on Lake Champlain and fought a British fleet at Valcour Island. He lost the battle, but the fight delayed the British invasion from Canada until the next year. That invasion ended at Saratoga, New York, in 1777. General Horatio Gates, the American commander there, had removed Arnold from command after a quarrel. On October 7, Arnold rode into the battle without orders and led attacks on the British lines. He was wounded again in the same leg. The British army surrendered on October 17. News of Saratoga helped convince France to join the war as an American ally in February 1778.</p>
